WEBVTT

00:02.770 --> 00:05.190
Feelings and memories…

00:05.560 --> 00:08.730
They exist only within my heart.

00:08.730 --> 00:12.150
Though we may pass the same time, or see the same sights,

00:12.150 --> 00:17.030
what we hold within our hearts can never be the same.

00:17.580 --> 00:20.240
Your face, your voice,

00:20.950 --> 00:23.580
the image of you, which exists only within me…

00:24.290 --> 00:27.130
Who are you?

00:28.540 --> 00:31.010
Faceless One

00:55.450 --> 00:59.780
The blue moon illuminated

00:59.830 --> 01:03.750
your wandering shadow.

01:04.370 --> 01:08.250
I could never tell you all I wanted to say.

01:08.250 --> 01:13.170
It was so very frustrating.

01:13.260 --> 01:17.050
I think about your faked smile,

01:17.640 --> 01:21.680
and forget all the hot tears we shed.

01:22.140 --> 01:24.350
What do these empty husks,

01:24.390 --> 01:30.190
those empty eyes of yours, reflect, my dear?

01:30.940 --> 01:35.400
The transient quarter moon

01:35.780 --> 01:37.570
hides in a rift in the clouds,

01:37.530 --> 01:39.950
as darkness seeps up from the ground.

01:39.990 --> 01:44.410
Tell me the truth, please.

01:44.750 --> 01:46.580
Are you so despondent

01:46.660 --> 01:50.960
that you still sit alone, sighing?

01:51.460 --> 01:54.420
Part the Second

02:04.350 --> 02:07.480
I’m afraid I won’t bend to your will.

02:09.730 --> 02:14.030
If you will not show me your true Form, then at least

02:14.030 --> 02:16.440
be quiet

02:17.030 --> 02:18.900
for a while.

02:18.900 --> 02:19.660
What?

02:20.410 --> 02:22.530
Please.

02:22.530 --> 02:24.290
What are you doing?

02:24.290 --> 02:25.450
Stop it!

02:38.840 --> 02:40.380
My, my.

02:42.180 --> 02:43.760
Such a contrary thing.

02:44.140 --> 02:49.310
Well then, shall we restart our little play?

02:49.850 --> 02:50.310
Play?

02:51.150 --> 02:56.780
The intertwined fates of men give the Mononoke its Form.

02:56.780 --> 03:03.990
When an Ayakashi clings onto
a person’s thoughts and feelings,

03:04.530 --> 03:07.660
it becomes a Mononoke.

03:05.740 --> 03:07.660
I see. You came here to kill the Mononoke.

03:07.660 --> 03:09.790
I see. You came here to kill the Mononoke.

03:09.790 --> 03:14.960
If I could kill it now, my work would be easy.

03:15.590 --> 03:20.550
I must discover the Mononoke’s Truth and Regret,

03:20.550 --> 03:23.010
and without its Form,

03:23.010 --> 03:25.890
I cannot draw the Sword of Exorcism.

03:30.310 --> 03:34.860
This is a troublesome Mononoke, indeed.

03:38.030 --> 03:40.740
Truth is a physical state,

03:41.240 --> 03:44.030
and Regret is a state of mind.

03:44.030 --> 03:47.160
If the Mononoke will not show me its Form,

03:47.740 --> 03:52.120
I will have to make it tell me

03:52.120 --> 03:56.920
its Truth and Regret.

04:00.710 --> 04:02.720
Ochou’s life,

04:04.010 --> 04:05.470
Part the First.

04:07.600 --> 04:10.180
My life?

04:10.180 --> 04:12.350
My life?

04:12.350 --> 04:15.270
Sake! Sake!

04:15.270 --> 04:16.560
I need more sake!

04:16.560 --> 04:20.190
I told you to bring me more sake! What are you doing?

04:20.190 --> 04:23.650
What a worthless wife you have.

04:23.650 --> 04:24.950
I’m sorry!

04:26.120 --> 04:31.660
The Mononoke is showing me what you feel.

04:41.380 --> 04:45.010
The perfect feelings for a Mononoke to leech.

04:45.430 --> 04:47.010
This is not a laughing matter!

04:47.010 --> 04:50.100
Yes it is. Quite funny, indeed.

04:51.600 --> 04:54.940
With such a laughable situation as an excuse,

04:56.900 --> 04:59.270
how many did you kill?

04:59.270 --> 05:00.480
how many did you kill?

05:05.320 --> 05:09.120
This is the result of relying on the Mononoke’s strength.

05:09.580 --> 05:10.580
Relying on…

05:10.950 --> 05:12.950
Do you remember that?

05:12.950 --> 05:14.160
Do you remember that?

05:18.580 --> 05:20.540
The sky?

05:20.540 --> 05:22.710
That’s right.

05:22.710 --> 05:23.880
The sky.

05:25.630 --> 05:28.720
Your very own sky,

05:28.720 --> 05:32.010
which you watched every day.

05:32.010 --> 05:34.680
My own sky?

05:34.680 --> 05:36.850
My own sky?

05:36.850 --> 05:40.810
I told you to bring me more sake! What are you doing?

05:40.810 --> 05:42.780
I—I’m sorry!

06:07.970 --> 06:11.760
You simply looked.

06:11.760 --> 06:14.810
I was only looking, but it made me happy.

06:14.810 --> 06:18.730
Why did you not leave this place?

06:18.730 --> 06:21.310
Stop it.

06:21.310 --> 06:25.900
Who is it that you really killed?

06:23.360 --> 06:25.900
Stop it.

06:27.070 --> 06:28.110
Stop it.

06:28.110 --> 06:32.030
Who did I really kill?

06:31.450 --> 06:32.030
Stop it!

06:32.030 --> 06:33.160
Stop it!

06:33.490 --> 06:34.660
Ochou-san,

06:37.540 --> 06:39.580
who did you kill?

06:39.580 --> 06:40.370
who did you kill?

06:44.590 --> 06:46.170
Stop it!

06:47.170 --> 06:52.970
Step no further into Ochou-san’s heart!

06:54.390 --> 06:56.560
Ochou-san,

06:56.560 --> 06:59.640
if you believe this place binds you, it will be your prison.

07:00.100 --> 07:02.650
If you do not wish to leave, it will become a fortress.

07:04.770 --> 07:07.320
It’s the same as that place.

07:09.240 --> 07:13.240
You thought of it as a prison.

07:16.040 --> 07:17.950
I…

07:19.290 --> 07:22.880
I told you to bring me more sake! What are you doing?

07:22.330 --> 07:22.880
I—I’m sorry!

07:22.880 --> 07:23.460
I—I’m sorry!

07:37.680 --> 07:41.640
Why did I not simply leave?

07:55.200 --> 07:56.410
Mother.

07:56.950 --> 08:00.330
You look just like I did when I was young.

08:00.790 --> 08:06.920
With your beauty, you will certainly
be able to marry into a wealthy family.

08:08.000 --> 08:09.090
Mother,

08:09.960 --> 08:12.970
I’ll do my best.

08:14.300 --> 08:18.060
This is most difficult.

08:22.520 --> 08:25.900
I loved my mother.

08:25.900 --> 08:28.110
Stop it, Ochou-san!

08:28.440 --> 08:30.530
You don’t have to tell him anything!

08:30.530 --> 08:32.740
He is deceiving you!

08:34.610 --> 08:35.820
Be quiet.

08:36.620 --> 08:39.080
The play is not over.

08:41.160 --> 08:43.830
Ochou’s life,

08:43.830 --> 08:44.830
Part the Second.

08:47.080 --> 08:50.840
You were born beautiful.

08:48.880 --> 08:50.130
What is this?

08:50.840 --> 08:54.760
Mind your appearance carefully,

08:51.710 --> 08:52.880
Mother?

08:54.760 --> 09:01.430
and you will be able to marry into a wealthy
family, in spite of your humble upbringing.

09:01.430 --> 09:03.430
Yes, Mother!

09:04.690 --> 09:08.400
Good girl. Good girl.

09:08.400 --> 09:11.980
I loved my mother.

09:12.480 --> 09:15.900
I wanted her praise.

09:15.900 --> 09:17.780
So you bore it,

09:18.950 --> 09:22.540
to the point of losing your own soul.

09:24.200 --> 09:26.580
My soul?

09:26.580 --> 09:27.330
My soul?

09:28.750 --> 09:30.630
How many times must I say it?

09:30.630 --> 09:32.090
I’m sorry!

09:32.090 --> 09:34.970
I’ve warned you about that so many times!

09:34.970 --> 09:36.510
I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry!

09:36.510 --> 09:38.640
I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry!

09:37.890 --> 09:38.640
Watch.

09:38.640 --> 09:39.930
I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry!

09:38.640 --> 09:41.220
Start over from the beginning.

09:39.930 --> 09:41.390
I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry!

09:41.390 --> 09:42.770
I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry!

09:43.180 --> 09:44.480
I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry!

09:44.100 --> 09:47.770
You’ll never be a proper lady at this rate!

09:44.480 --> 09:46.140
I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry!

09:46.140 --> 09:47.770
I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry!

09:47.770 --> 09:49.520
I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry!

09:48.850 --> 09:49.810
One more time!

09:49.520 --> 09:51.020
I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry! I’m sorry!

09:51.020 --> 09:51.860
Yes.

10:03.990 --> 10:05.040
No.

10:06.620 --> 10:07.830
No.

10:07.830 --> 10:10.790
One and two and three!

10:08.790 --> 10:10.210
No.

10:11.630 --> 10:14.800
Four and five and six!

10:12.130 --> 10:13.250
No.

10:15.130 --> 10:18.880
Seven and eight and nine!

10:15.170 --> 10:16.670
No.

10:19.760 --> 10:21.470
Stop this.

10:22.850 --> 10:26.930
I hid myself, so as not to interrupt your taking of vows.

10:28.730 --> 10:29.850
Mother.

10:30.350 --> 10:32.900
Ochou’s life,

10:32.900 --> 10:34.070
Part the Third.

10:34.780 --> 10:38.110
I merely wish to express my
gratitude and extend my best wishes.

10:38.110 --> 10:39.700
Thank you. Thank you so much.

10:39.700 --> 10:42.370
Please, sit up now.

10:42.370 --> 10:45.910
We derive no pleasure from watching you prostrate yourself.

10:46.290 --> 10:48.460
My goodness, such a gorgeous lady she is.

10:48.460 --> 10:50.540
Are you as good in bed as you look?

10:50.540 --> 10:51.830
Oh my, stop it!

10:51.830 --> 10:53.880
That’s for our brother to find out!

10:54.920 --> 10:57.630
I can buy as many women as I want with money.

10:57.970 --> 11:00.470
Please! Please!

11:00.880 --> 11:07.930
Please, keep her for all her life!

11:02.180 --> 11:05.100
Is this your mother’s wish?

11:05.100 --> 11:06.140
Yes.

11:06.140 --> 11:07.930
My father died young, and his pension was confiscated.

11:07.930 --> 11:09.390
My father died young, and his pension was confiscated.

11:09.770 --> 11:14.820
All my mother wished was for me to marry into wealth.

11:14.820 --> 11:18.110
That was the only thing she wished for.

11:18.110 --> 11:25.830
Now I can finally hold my head high as I visit
the graves of my ancestors, the Umezawake clan.

11:25.830 --> 11:27.410
I see.

11:27.410 --> 11:33.830
So, you became your mother’s tool, to further her ends.

11:32.210 --> 11:33.830
No!

11:33.830 --> 11:36.250
Then, what is that?

11:49.390 --> 11:50.850
Again?

11:51.440 --> 11:55.690
You lost your soul for your mother’s wish.

11:56.520 --> 12:02.490
You became a tool for your mother’s selfish ends.

12:02.490 --> 12:04.160
Then, you fell in love.

12:04.160 --> 12:06.070
You…

12:06.450 --> 12:11.330
But the object of your affections…

12:11.330 --> 12:12.210
Who was he?

12:12.210 --> 12:13.250
What?

12:13.250 --> 12:16.170
Ochou’s life,

12:16.170 --> 12:17.590
Part the Fourth.

12:17.590 --> 12:21.720
I told you to bring me more sake! What are you doing?

12:21.720 --> 12:23.130
I—I’m sorry!

12:23.130 --> 12:27.100
Ochou-san, just get us some more sake!

12:27.100 --> 12:29.510
What a worthless wife you have.

12:30.310 --> 12:32.140
A lazy girl, indeed.

12:32.140 --> 12:35.810
Brother, whyever did you take her in?

12:35.810 --> 12:39.820
Her mother begged me to.

12:39.820 --> 12:45.700
If your first wife hadn’t hung herself, would
you ever have accepted her into your home?

12:45.700 --> 12:48.160
Well, she’s a pretty good cook,

12:48.160 --> 12:51.620
and good in bed, too!

12:51.620 --> 12:54.670
Oh stop, you’re just terrible!

13:11.970 --> 13:14.390
Ochou-san,

13:14.390 --> 13:17.270
who did you kill?

13:19.980 --> 13:21.530
Stop it.

13:24.240 --> 13:25.530
Stop it.

13:27.780 --> 13:28.950
Stop it.

13:30.330 --> 13:31.580
Stop it.

13:33.330 --> 13:34.370
Stop it.

13:35.410 --> 13:37.210
Stop it! Stop it!

13:38.000 --> 13:40.420
Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!

13:42.670 --> 13:46.840
Stop it!

13:49.050 --> 13:52.640
Stop it. Stop it.

13:57.940 --> 13:59.900
Ochou-san,

13:59.900 --> 14:01.440
that mask is not

14:02.320 --> 14:05.940
a Mononoke.

14:06.780 --> 14:09.530
A Mononoke controls the masked man.

14:09.530 --> 14:12.740
A Mononoke controls the masked man.

14:12.740 --> 14:14.290
It deceived you,

14:14.620 --> 14:17.000
and imprisoned you.

14:19.460 --> 14:22.130
That is its Truth.

14:26.920 --> 14:28.630
Lies.

14:28.630 --> 14:31.800
And in trying to accept your mother’s twisted love,

14:31.800 --> 14:35.890
And in trying to accept your mother’s twisted love,

14:33.180 --> 14:35.020
No! No! No! No! No! No!

14:35.020 --> 14:37.060
No! No! No! No! No! No!

14:35.890 --> 14:40.650
your heart wavered, and a Mononoke latched onto it.

14:37.060 --> 14:38.190
No! No! No! No! No! No!

14:38.190 --> 14:39.600
No! No! No! No! No! No!

14:39.600 --> 14:40.650
No! No! No! No! No! No!

14:40.650 --> 14:43.820
That is the Regret.

14:40.650 --> 14:42.940
No! No! No! No! No! No!

14:51.320 --> 14:56.200
I loved my mother.

14:56.200 --> 14:59.410
Mother, look!

14:59.410 --> 15:02.250
You’re so beautiful.

15:02.250 --> 15:06.050
You can fulfill my dream and marry into wealth.

15:02.630 --> 15:06.050
I did my best.

15:06.050 --> 15:08.420
I did my best, but…

15:08.420 --> 15:11.090
No! No! No!

15:12.260 --> 15:15.510
No! No more.

15:15.510 --> 15:19.310
Mother, listen! Listen to me!

15:20.230 --> 15:23.150
Mother, listen to me!

15:20.230 --> 15:23.150
I can’t wait!

15:23.150 --> 15:26.480
Mother, listen to me!

15:23.940 --> 15:26.480
Why won’t you listen to what I have to say?

15:26.480 --> 15:29.070
Why won’t you listen to what I have to say?

15:29.070 --> 15:31.150
Mother, listen to me!

15:31.820 --> 15:36.410
All four of these men are wealthy and prosperous.

15:33.530 --> 15:36.410
Mother, why won’t you listen to me?

15:36.410 --> 15:39.330
Mother, why won’t you listen to me?

15:42.500 --> 15:43.250
Listen…

15:43.250 --> 15:46.590
I can’t wait. I can’t wait…

15:44.170 --> 15:46.590
Listen…

15:46.590 --> 15:49.050
I can’t wait. I can’t wait…

15:46.590 --> 15:49.050
Listen to me.

15:49.670 --> 15:52.880
I can’t wait. I can’t wait…

15:51.340 --> 15:52.510
I…

15:52.880 --> 15:56.890
I can’t wait. I can’t wait…

15:54.010 --> 15:55.680
I…

15:57.140 --> 15:58.470
I…

16:02.480 --> 16:04.100
I’m so stupid.

16:04.100 --> 16:05.440
Ochou.

16:07.570 --> 16:11.320
Who was it that you killed?

16:11.320 --> 16:12.110
Who was it that you killed?

16:14.530 --> 16:16.870
Who did I

16:17.780 --> 16:19.580
kill?

16:29.800 --> 16:32.550
All of them

16:35.680 --> 16:37.680
were me?

16:42.390 --> 16:43.810
I…

16:44.310 --> 16:49.690
You lost yourself in others’ greed.

16:45.440 --> 16:47.190
Why?

16:49.690 --> 16:50.400
I…

16:50.400 --> 16:52.690
You are a Mononoke.

16:52.690 --> 16:53.570
Show me

16:56.070 --> 16:57.280
your Form.

17:03.620 --> 17:04.580
It’s me!

17:07.170 --> 17:08.670
I am

17:10.960 --> 17:12.300
the Mononoke!

17:28.980 --> 17:31.400
May I ask you one thing?

17:31.400 --> 17:32.820
May I ask you one thing?

17:36.240 --> 17:38.530
Why did the Faceless One…

17:46.250 --> 17:49.920
Why did it save me?

17:49.920 --> 17:54.260
Do you believe you were saved?

18:00.220 --> 18:02.640
If you wish to know,

18:03.100 --> 18:05.850
perhaps it fell in love

18:09.650 --> 18:11.560
with you.

18:13.480 --> 18:15.940
His love could never be.

18:15.940 --> 18:18.910
The Mononoke despaired.

18:18.910 --> 18:19.950
The Mononoke despaired.

18:21.740 --> 18:25.080
The Mononoke despaired?

18:25.080 --> 18:26.870
The Mononoke despaired?

18:36.670 --> 18:38.300
Thank you.

18:44.100 --> 18:46.520
Thank you.

18:46.520 --> 18:48.060
I’ll be fine.

18:55.570 --> 18:59.110
I told you to bring me more sake! What are you doing?

18:59.110 --> 19:00.820
I—I’m sorry!

19:00.820 --> 19:04.370
Ochou-san, just get us some more sake!

19:04.370 --> 19:07.000
What a worthless wife you have.

19:07.620 --> 19:09.250
A lazy girl, indeed.

19:09.250 --> 19:12.380
Brother, whyever did you take her in?

19:13.210 --> 19:16.250
Her mother begged me to.

19:16.250 --> 19:22.220
If your first wife hadn’t hung herself, would
you ever have accepted her into your home?

19:22.220 --> 19:24.970
Well, she’s a pretty good cook,

19:24.970 --> 19:27.850
and good in bed, too!

19:27.850 --> 19:31.020
Oh stop, you’re just terrible!

19:59.380 --> 20:02.510
Hey, what are you doing?

20:05.140 --> 20:06.550
Lazy bitch.

20:06.550 --> 20:09.060
You’re totally useless.

20:09.060 --> 20:11.140
Indeed, she is.

20:11.140 --> 20:12.350
She’s so damned lazy.

20:12.350 --> 20:13.940
Hey!

20:13.520 --> 20:16.110
Useless indeed.

20:13.940 --> 20:15.480
Ochou!

20:15.480 --> 20:18.780
Can’t you hear?

20:18.780 --> 20:20.360
Still not here?

20:20.360 --> 20:25.820
She lazes around so, whatever she does.

20:25.820 --> 20:27.830
I just can’t stand her!

20:27.830 --> 20:31.700
What’s taking her so long, I wonder?

20:31.700 --> 20:33.420
Ochou!

20:33.420 --> 20:35.580
Sake! Sake!

20:35.580 --> 20:37.170
Bring us sake!

20:39.840 --> 20:42.050
Where’s the sake?

20:42.050 --> 20:44.760
But there’s no-one here.

20:44.760 --> 20:46.800
But there’s no-one here.

20:46.800 --> 20:47.970
But there’s no-one here.

21:04.490 --> 21:09.950
The End

21:11.750 --> 21:19.250
Without you, I just can’t smile.

21:20.380 --> 21:30.310
I walk this banal town,

21:30.310 --> 21:36.390
feeling such intense emotions.

21:36.940 --> 21:42.780
I know that if I could treasure them and live on,

21:42.860 --> 21:52.080
I would need nothing else.

21:52.740 --> 22:00.250
The summer flowers that bloomed in the sky

22:00.250 --> 22:06.550
Come falling down, dancing in the wind.

22:06.630 --> 22:09.890
I can barely recall the night sky

22:09.890 --> 22:13.180
where they all came tumbling down,

22:13.180 --> 22:24.030
so what I can still recall is all the more precious.
